--- A literal list compared with a list of ints that may grow past 64 bits
--- compares their numbers, as with any list of numbers: compiled, a tensor
--- had been compared with a list of growing ints by Rust's `==`, and did
--- not build (Rosetta Code, Bernoulli's triangle).
fn growing[n]
    out = []
    c = 1
    for k in range[n]
        out = push[out, c]
        c = c * 3
    return out

row = [1, 3]
log[row eq growing[2]]
log[row ne growing[3]]
